l is 29% over 1 year, 30% over 6 months and 31% over 3 months.\n- That puts implied about 17–23% below realized, so you pay less vol premium than recent history would justify.\n- Long-dated implied vol usually sits below short-term realized vol because vol tends to mean-revert. Part of the gap may therefore be fair, not a bargain.\n- The skew is mild. 110% strike calls are the cheapest at 23.5%, against 25.5% at 90%.\n\n**Policy path** (n4.r1)\n- The CMA policy rate is 4.50% and was held at the October meeting.\n- Futures price a first cut by 2027Q2 and a second by Q4, about 50bp in total, ending at 4.00%.\n- Governor Ashby's base case is a single 25bp cut in 2027, which means a rate near 4.25%. The market is pricing about one cut more than the CMA signals.\n- The futures curve ends at 2027Q4, so I have no market pricing for January 2028.\n\n**What this means for the calls**\n- A long-dated call is sensitive to rates through the forward and rho, and the options note says so. If the CMA delivers fewer cuts than priced, rates stay higher than the market expects. That slightly favors the call's carry and forward, but it could weigh on the rate-sensitive holdings and on the equity value.\n- The earnings backdrop is neutral to supportive. Consensus expects 14% EPS growth for VLTX holdings in 2027 (doc vltx-earnings-2027), but that was not tested here.\n- The main limit is that I can't compare premium to breakeven or to a fair value. Check actual bid/ask prices and the delta of the strike before acting.","ttft_ms":2792,"type":"result","duration_ms":35760,"uuid":"77b02e2d-b567-4f61-be6b-fe93a1a401c0","ttft_stream_ms":1141,"time_to_request_ms":66,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"re